    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:154`). All owner-specific logic is imperative code inside the controller \u2014 the service layer (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`) is a thin pass-through with no validation, and the `Owner` entity has **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.).\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`: caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, or the method is never entered.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, checked before dispatch. Per-field constraints (on `OwnerFieldsDto`):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/'/- separated words)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (similar, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern ^[0-9 ()+.-]*$` (loose \u2014 validated on the **raw** input, not the E.164 form)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` only (optional; **no** `@NotNull`, **no** `@Email`)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 ISO date format\n   - `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraints\n   - No custom `ConstraintValidator` applies to owners (the only custom one, `PetAgeValidator`, is for pets).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Inside `addOwner` (exact source order)\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` (MapStruct; ignores `pets` and `id`; does **not** map `sharesHousehold`).\n4. **Future-date validation** \u2014 if supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Default + normalize registration date** \u2014 default to today if null; roll weekend forward to next business day (`toBusinessDay`); store on entity. *(side-effect: sets `registrationDate`)*\n6. **Daily volume cap** \u2014 count owners already registered on that date (`findAllOwners()`); if `>= 100` \u2192 **429**.\n7. **Bulk-signup warning flag** \u2014 set `bulkSignupWarning = (createdToday > 80)`. *(side-effect)*\n8. **Address normalization + validation** \u2014 trim/collapse/uppercase/expand abbreviations (`normalizeAddress`); if empty \u2192 **400**; store. *(side-effect: rewrites `address`)*\n9. **Telephone normalization + validation** \u2014 convert to E.164 (`toE164`); if invalid \u2192 **400**; store. *(side-effect: rewrites `telephone`)*\n10. **Email (only if present)** \u2014 normalize (trim + lowercase); if fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` regex \u2192 **400**; if disposable domain (`isDisposableEmailDomain`) \u2192 **400**; store. *(side-effect: rewrites `email`)*\n11. **Postcode/region consistency** \u2014 `isPostcodeValidForCity(postcode, locality)`; if mismatch \u2192 **400**.\n12. **City household cap** \u2014 count owners in the same normalized city (`findAllOwners()`); if `>= 50` \u2192 **409**.\n13. **Household assignment** \u2014 compute `householdId` (SHA-256 of normalized lastName + postcode), store; compute `householdSize = existing members + 1`, store. *(side-effects)*\n14. **Household-sharing check** \u2014 read `sharesHousehold` **directly from the DTO**; if an existing household member exists and `!sharesHousehold` \u2192 **409**.\n15. **Identity uniqueness** \u2014 compute `identityKey` (telephone|email|householdId); if any existing owner matches \u2192 **409**.\n16. **Soft-duplicate detection** (skipped if `sharesHousehold`) \u2014 find an existing owner with same normalized lastName + same postcode + *different* telephone; if found set `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = <id>`, else `possibleDuplicate = false`. *(side-effects)*\n17. **Customer code** \u2014 set `customerCode` = `<region>-<8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName)>`. *(side-effect)*\n18. **Namesake count** \u2014 count owners with same first+last name; store `namesakeCount`. *(side-effect)*\n19. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `em.persist` (new row; IDENTITY-generated id). `Owner.pets` has `cascade=ALL` but the collection is empty here, so nothing cascades.\n20. **Audit log** \u2014 one line on the `\"AUDIT\"` SLF4J logger: `owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...`. *(side-effect)*\n21. **Response** \u2014 map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notable structural facts\n\n- **No transaction spans the create.** `addOwner` is **not** `@Transactional`. Each of the ~6 `findAllOwners()` reads runs in its own read-only transaction, and `saveOwner` runs in a separate one \u2014 so all the count/uniqueness/duplicate checks (steps 6, 12, 13, 15, 16, 18) and the insert are **not atomic** and are subject to races.\n- **No events, no emails.** No `ApplicationEventPublisher`/`@EventListener`, no `JavaMailSender` \u2014 the only \"email\" logic is the disposable-domain rejection; nothing is actually sent. Audit logging is the only external-facing side-effect besides the DB write.\n- **No password encoding / entity callbacks / auto-timestamping** \u2014 every derived column is set explicitly in the controller before save.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the telephone is Bean-Validated against a loose pattern on the *raw* DTO value, but the strict E.164 pattern lives on the `Owner` **entity** field, which is never re-validated on the JPA path \u2014 so the only real E.164 enforcement is the imperative `toE164` check at step 9."
